Here is a (likely incomplete) list of changes I've made to the original
xv6-riscv repository:

## Kernel

I've added several more system calls: `time()`, `lseek()`, `ioctl()`.
The kernel now returns `errno` values as well as the usual system call
results. I fixed an `sbrk()` bug. I added ECHO and ICANON flags to the
console. I added more stack pages to each process space as well as an
invalid page to catch NULL pointer dereferences.

## Libraries

I've moved the xv6 libraries into `lib/ulib/`, and I've imported
the FUZIX libraries into `lib/libc`. I've had to make some adjustments
to some of the FUZIX functions to match a) the 32-bit RISC-V environment
and b) the xv6 kernel.

There are also several functions in the `lib/stub` directory which
either provide dummy actions, e.g. `access()`, or help interface the
FUZIX libraries with the xv6 kernel, e.g. `fstat().

## Userland

`cmds/xv6/` now contain the original xv6 programs. `cmds/simple/` hold
commands from FUZIX which fit into one file each. The other directories
in `cmd/` are for programs which have multiple source files.

## Organisation

I've restructured the organisation of the source code into more
directories, and created Makefiles so that the code in each
sub-directory can be built, installed and cleaned.

## Tools

`mkfs` now builds a filesystem image based on the contents of
a directory. The `fs/` directory is used as the source directory.
